Nc6
{ [%eval 0.43] Defends e5 and develops a piece. White now chooses between the Italian, the Three Knights and the Scotch. }
3. Bc4
{ [%eval 0.18] The Italian Game. The bishop looks at f7, Black's weakest square. }
( 3. Nc3
{ [%eval 0.16] The Three Knights. White develops a third piece before deciding on a plan. }
3... Nf6
{ [%eval 0.13] After 3...Nf6 this is the Four Knights Game. It is solid and rather drawish: Black just copies White's development and there is no need to look for more. }
4. Bb5 { [%eval 0.04] The Spanish-style move, aimed at the c6 knight. } ( 4. d4
{ [%eval 0.13] White opens the centre at once. } 4... exd4
{ [%eval 0.14] Black takes. } 5. Nxd4
