Nxc6 { [%eval 0.18] White trades a pair of knights. } 6... bxc6
{ [%eval 0.19] Black recaptures. The pawn structure is a little worse but the bishops are active. }
7. Bd3 { [%eval 0.15] White develops. } 7... d5
{ [%eval 0.14] Black strikes in the centre. } 8. exd5
{ [%eval 0.15] White takes. } 8... cxd5 $10
{ [%eval 0.15] Black recaptures and the position is level. } ) 4... Bb4
{ [%eval 0.20] Black pins in return. This is the Four Knights Spanish: a symmetrical pin on both sides. Black copies White's setup, which is solid and easy to play. }
