{ [%eval 0.52] White takes the pawn back. } 7... Bb6 $14
{ [%eval 0.50] The bishop steps back to a safe diagonal and stays aimed at d4 and f2. }
) 4... Nf6 { [%eval 0.19] Develops with an attack on e4. } 5. Nxc6
{ [%eval 0.18] White removes the c6 knight. } 5... bxc6
{ [%eval 0.13] Black recaptures with the b-pawn, and this is the only good way. Taking with 5...dxc6? allows 6.Qxd8+ Kxd8, and Black has lost the right to castle. The doubled c-pawns control d5 and open the b-file. }
6. e5 { [%eval 0.04] White pushes with tempo, attacking the knight. } 6... Qe7
{ [%eval 0.00] The Mieses Variation, which Kasparov played with Black. The queen attacks e5 and prepares ...Nd5, and the pin on the e-file makes White decide what to do with the pawn on e5. }
7. Qe2 { [%eval 0.00] White unpins and defends e5. } 7... Nd5
{ [%eval 0.00] The knight goes to the centre. It is safe there and eyes c3 and f4. }
8. c4 { [%eval 0.00] White kicks the knight. } 8... Ba6 $10
{ [%eval -0.02] The bishop pins the queen to the king and pushes a trade of queens that favours Black. A strong move. }
) 3... Bc5
{ [%eval 0.23] [%cal Gc5f2] The Giuoco Piano. Black mirrors White: the bishop takes the matching diagonal and eyes f2. }
( 3... Nf6
{ [%eval 0.22] The Two Knights. Black develops with an attack on e4 and leaves the bishop at home for now. }
4. Ng5
{ [%eval 0.23] An aggressive try at f7. It looks scary, and the only way to meet it is to counter in the centre at once. }
4... d5
{ [%eval 0.23] [%cal Gd7d5] Black must hit the centre. Defending passively with ...Nxe4 or ...Qe7 loses time or material. }
5. exd5 { [%eval 0.16] White takes the pawn. } 5... Na5
{ [%eval 0.15] [%cal Gc6a5] The right recapture. Taking with the knight (...Nxd5) walks into 6.Nxf7, the Fried Liver, a trap that wins for White. The knight on a5 hits the bishop instead. }
6. Bb5+ { [%eval 0.14] White checks and tries to keep the extra pawn. } 6... c6
{ [%eval 0.21] Blocks the check and attacks the pawn on d5 and the bishop. } 7.
dxc6 { [%eval 0.17] White takes. } 7... bxc6
{ [%eval 0.15] Black takes back and attacks the bishop on b5. } 8. Be2
{ [%eval 0.01] The bishop retreats. } 8... h6
