{ [%eval 0.20] The quiet Giuoco Pianissimo, the "very quiet game". White builds slowly with d3, Nbd2 and O-O, and keeps the centre solid. There is less theory than in the sharp lines, so it is easy to play well with a simple plan. }
( 5. d4 { [%eval 0.02] White strikes in the centre at once. } 5... exd4
{ [%eval 0.02] Takes the pawn. After cxd4 Black has the check ...Bb4+, which is why taking on d4 is the right choice here and not something to avoid. }
6. cxd4
{ [%eval 0.02] White recaptures and has a big pawn centre, with a check coming. }
6... Bb4+
