9. exd5 { [%eval 0.08] White takes. } 9... Nxd5 $10
{ [%eval 0.16] Black recaptures with a piece, aims at the isolated pawn on d4 and keeps the knights active. }
) 5... d6
{ [%eval 0.24] Supports e5 and opens the c8 bishop. Black's usual plan from here is ...a6 or ...a5, then ...O-O: keep the centre solid, castle, and wait for White to make a commitment. }
6. O-O { [%eval 0.24] White castles. } 6... O-O $10
{ [%eval 0.18] Black castles too. Both sides are developed and both kings are safe; what follows is a manoeuvring game. }
